{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2fCNc1mQYehdKns432","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The export package now uses a plugin registry. Adding a format means adding one module under `export/formats/`; `core.py` does not change. The full suite passes: 9 tests, the 5 existing ones plus 4 new registry tests.\n\n**What changed** (in `t10_plugin_registry/`):\n\n- **`export/registry.py`** (new): the `Exporter` ABC with `name`, `extension` (leading dot, as before), and `dump(records)`. It also holds the registry:\n  - `register` works as a decorator and rejects a duplicate name bound to a different class.\n  - `get(name)` returns an exporter instance and raises `UnknownFormat`, whose message lists the known names.\n  - `names()` returns the sorted names.\n  - `UnknownFormat` moved here and is still a `ValueError` subclass, so `export.UnknownFormat` works as before.\n- **`export/formats/`** (new): `csv_format.py`, `json_format.py`, `xml_format.py`, each registering one `Exporter`. `__init__.py` imports every module in the package via `pkgutil`, so the formats register on `import export`.\n- **`export/core.py`**: `export_records` and `export_to_file` keep their signatures. Both now look up the exporter in the registry, with no if-chains. Output bytes and file-extension behaviour are unchanged.\n- **`export/__init__.py`**: imports the formats and re-exports the existing names, plus `Exporter`, `register`, `get`, and `names`.\n- **`tests/test_registry.py`** (new): built-in names, the unknown-format message, registering a new format without touching core, and duplicate-name rejection.\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to change:**\n\n- Module names are `*_format.py` rather than `csv.py`/`json.py`/`xml.py`, to avoid confusion with stdlib modules.\n- `get` returns an instance, not the class, since exporters are stateless.\n- Re-registering a different class under an existing name raises `ValueError` instead of silently replacing it.\n\nI did not commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4322,"cache_read_input_tokens":57973,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4322},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b12ace90-9029-40d4-aaf3-d34b658f4db0","uuid":"633d0922-1fc1-4a91-a1d1-e6e4753302f1","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:06:55.759Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2fBwogxaK7b2Arg2xX"}
